WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.520 --> 00:00:04.890
Welcome to "Ear Biscuits,"

00:00:04.890 --> 00:00:06.750
the podcast for two lifelong friends

00:00:06.750 --> 00:00:09.280
talk about life for a long time.

00:00:09.280 --> 00:00:10.113
I'm Link.

00:00:10.113 --> 00:00:10.946
And I'm Rhett.

00:00:10.946 --> 00:00:12.790
This week at the round
table of dim lighting,

00:00:12.790 --> 00:00:17.623
we are celebrating 10 years
of "Good Mythical Morning."

00:00:17.623 --> 00:00:20.530
It's a show that we make
other than this show.

00:00:20.530 --> 00:00:22.550
It's on a platform called YouTube.

00:00:22.550 --> 00:00:24.560
Apparently we've been
making it on that platform

00:00:24.560 --> 00:00:28.100
for 10 years, and last week we did

00:00:28.100 --> 00:00:32.180
a celebration week on the show,

00:00:32.180 --> 00:00:36.540
and we're capping that off
with a lengthy discussion.

00:00:36.540 --> 00:00:37.840
Of retrospective.
Looking back

00:00:37.840 --> 00:00:41.246
on the length of "Good Mythical Morning."

00:00:41.246 --> 00:00:42.996
Ten years.
It's not just length.

00:00:43.924 --> 00:00:44.834
Link.

00:00:44.834 --> 00:00:46.210
What?
Could you not use length?

00:00:46.210 --> 00:00:47.381
However, we have established

00:00:47.381 --> 00:00:51.163
that your porn name would
be Length Neal, right?

00:00:52.690 --> 00:00:53.523
Did we?

00:00:53.523 --> 00:00:54.970
I don't know if we've
ever said that publicly,

00:00:54.970 --> 00:00:56.820
but we discovered that at some point.

00:00:59.405 --> 00:01:01.404
Well, how did you discover this, Rhett?

00:01:01.404 --> 00:01:02.380
This is getting weird.

00:01:02.380 --> 00:01:04.793
It was a conversation.

00:01:05.630 --> 00:01:08.190
It was a conversation
amongst friends, I believe.

00:01:08.190 --> 00:01:09.249
I don't know, maybe it was,

00:01:09.249 --> 00:01:11.300
you probably know, it may have been

00:01:11.300 --> 00:01:12.689
on "Good Mythical More."
I think it happened

00:01:12.689 --> 00:01:14.240
at this table.

00:01:14.240 --> 00:01:15.073
Really?

00:01:15.073 --> 00:01:15.906
Length Neal

00:01:15.906 --> 00:01:17.284
was born at this table?
I think so.

00:01:17.284 --> 00:01:21.490
So, my idea, I've done some homework here.

00:01:21.490 --> 00:01:23.430
I've looked back.

00:01:23.430 --> 00:01:24.530
Well, let me just give you

00:01:24.530 --> 00:01:26.060
my perspective on what you told me,

00:01:26.060 --> 00:01:30.020
because we were gonna do
a retrospective episode,

00:01:30.020 --> 00:01:31.420
and, you know, we actually,

00:01:31.420 --> 00:01:33.480
over the summer, we did
the retrospective episode

00:01:33.480 --> 00:01:37.690
of 2000 episodes of GMM, which
happened over the summer.

00:01:37.690 --> 00:01:39.501
This is when we were like,

00:01:39.501 --> 00:01:40.860
we're gonna do the same thing,

00:01:40.860 --> 00:01:42.810
so we were trying to figure out other ways

00:01:42.810 --> 00:01:45.140
to talk about this much GMM

00:01:45.140 --> 00:01:47.900
without dipping back into
the same conversation.

00:01:47.900 --> 00:01:48.733
Yeah.

00:01:48.733 --> 00:01:50.984
It's a lot of conversation
about fan evolution

00:01:50.984 --> 00:01:52.322
in that episode.
Right.

00:01:52.322 --> 00:01:53.155
And...

00:01:54.280 --> 00:01:56.807
So, we were talking like,

00:01:56.807 --> 00:01:58.300
"Okay, we'll think about it over break."

00:01:58.300 --> 00:02:00.507
And so then when we got back, you said,

00:02:00.507 --> 00:02:05.507
"Well, I kinda went back to the beginning,

00:02:05.820 --> 00:02:08.823
and started looking at
titles and thumbnails."

00:02:08.823 --> 00:02:09.897
Just to jog my memory.

00:02:09.897 --> 00:02:14.897
"And then I just went through all of them,

00:02:15.280 --> 00:02:17.550
all 10 years worth of them."

00:02:17.550 --> 00:02:18.430
And you were like-
Yeah.

00:02:18.430 --> 00:02:20.270
And it took off, and made notes.

00:02:20.270 --> 00:02:21.103
And you were like,

00:02:21.103 --> 00:02:22.520
"And it took a lot longer
than I anticipated."

00:02:22.520 --> 00:02:24.190
I was like, yeah, over two-thirds.

00:02:24.190 --> 00:02:25.820
I mean, you could have, like.

00:02:25.820 --> 00:02:26.720
I didn't realize that

00:02:26.720 --> 00:02:28.050
I was signing myself in.
Ten episodes in,

00:02:28.050 --> 00:02:30.870
you could've extrapolated
and done the math length.

00:02:30.870 --> 00:02:31.760
Yeah.

00:02:31.760 --> 00:02:33.890
And figured out how much
length this was gonna take.

00:02:33.890 --> 00:02:36.020
I feel like I really, you know,

00:02:36.020 --> 00:02:40.410
I owed it to us in reminiscing

00:02:40.410 --> 00:02:43.090
and celebrating what we've done,

00:02:43.090 --> 00:02:44.290
what we've gone through,

00:02:45.130 --> 00:02:47.783
and what we've created, and what's evolved

00:02:47.783 --> 00:02:49.142
on "Good Mythical Morning."
Oh, I'm glad you did it.

00:02:49.142 --> 00:02:49.975
I'm glad you did it.
Over the years,

00:02:49.975 --> 00:02:51.067
I just want-
You can call me and say,

00:02:51.067 --> 00:02:54.340
"Could you start from the
end and meet in the middle?

00:02:54.340 --> 00:02:56.960
You just let me worry about other things."

00:02:56.960 --> 00:02:58.050
Well, it was just fascinating,

00:02:58.050 --> 00:03:00.560
because, I mean, with 10 years,

00:03:00.560 --> 00:03:03.710
at a certain point, the
show is just, it's a staple.

00:03:03.710 --> 00:03:05.040
It's a part of our lives,

00:03:05.040 --> 00:03:07.550
it's something that we go to the desk,

00:03:07.550 --> 00:03:11.742
we enter that zone, and we, you know...

00:03:11.742 --> 00:03:16.273
There's a rhythm to it that
it can kind of wash over you,

00:03:16.273 --> 00:03:19.847
like, I'm a little
self-conscious when we talk about

00:03:19.847 --> 00:03:20.680
"Good Mythical Morning,"

00:03:20.680 --> 00:03:22.530
because I know that mythical beasts,

00:03:22.530 --> 00:03:25.300
when you experience it as a viewer,

00:03:25.300 --> 00:03:29.820
it's different than how we
experienced it creating it.

00:03:29.820 --> 00:03:31.900
And we got to a point

00:03:31.900 --> 00:03:33.640
where we don't go back and watch it

00:03:33.640 --> 00:03:35.682
after the fact.
But also,

00:03:35.682 --> 00:03:37.183
because we registered.
Many, many years ago,

00:03:37.183 --> 00:03:38.016
we stopped doing that.

00:03:38.016 --> 00:03:40.060
And I think you probably
have picked up on this

00:03:40.060 --> 00:03:42.700
as we've talked about
the show over the years,

00:03:42.700 --> 00:03:45.480
the moments don't register with us

00:03:45.480 --> 00:03:48.200
in the same way that they
register with the audience.

00:03:48.200 --> 00:03:49.033
Yeah.

00:03:49.033 --> 00:03:50.060
Because...

00:03:52.150 --> 00:03:52.983
I don't know.

00:03:52.983 --> 00:03:54.977
It's kind of overwhelming for
us in that it's just like,

00:03:54.977 --> 00:03:56.410
"What's the craziest
thing you've ever eaten?

00:03:56.410 --> 00:03:58.100
What's the craziest thing
that ever happened on GM.

00:03:58.100 --> 00:03:58.933
Do you remember when you did this?"

00:03:58.933 --> 00:04:00.138
I was like,

00:04:00.138 --> 00:04:00.971
when you point it out-
What's your favorite

00:04:00.971 --> 00:04:01.804
episode? Yeah.

00:04:01.804 --> 00:04:03.780
But like, when I'm gonna bed at night,

00:04:03.780 --> 00:04:06.350
my mind is not filled with memories

00:04:06.350 --> 00:04:08.623
of the crazy stuff that we do on the show.

00:04:10.250 --> 00:04:12.866
It has to sort of be called out.

00:04:12.866 --> 00:04:16.250
So I have a feeling that when
you go through these things,

00:04:16.250 --> 00:04:18.090
I'm gonna be like, "Oh man, we did that?

00:04:18.090 --> 00:04:19.322
Hell, we did that."

00:04:19.322 --> 00:04:21.090
I wouldn't have thought about that again

00:04:21.090 --> 00:04:22.210
if you didn't point it out.

00:04:22.210 --> 00:04:25.270
And I was particularly fascinated

00:04:25.270 --> 00:04:28.110
with how the show has evolved,

00:04:28.110 --> 00:04:31.710
