that's when we broke
a million subscribers.

00:43:42.350 --> 00:43:43.950
Well, one of the things that I'm seeing

00:43:43.950 --> 00:43:48.280
in the numbers here is that, season five.

00:43:48.280 --> 00:43:51.870
So they're seeing like,
towards the end of season four,

00:43:51.870 --> 00:43:55.010
okay, we're getting...

00:43:55.010 --> 00:43:56.730
Some stuff is really taking off.

00:43:56.730 --> 00:43:58.890
Some stuff is really getting traction.

00:43:58.890 --> 00:44:02.550
Season five, so seven years ago.

00:44:02.550 --> 00:44:03.383
Yeah.

00:44:03.383 --> 00:44:04.216
That's when...

00:44:04.216 --> 00:44:06.620
That has to be, based on
the numbers that I'm seeing,

00:44:06.620 --> 00:44:08.950
that has to be the
beginning of what we called

00:44:08.950 --> 00:44:11.830
the YouTube algorithm change
that we've benefited from,

00:44:11.830 --> 00:44:14.790
where they started rewarding watch time.

00:44:14.790 --> 00:44:15.623
Yeah.

00:44:15.623 --> 00:44:17.500
Doesn't that sound about
like the beginning of that,

00:44:17.500 --> 00:44:18.800
seven years ago?

00:44:18.800 --> 00:44:20.080
So like, 2015?

00:44:20.080 --> 00:44:22.950
Yeah, 'cause we got a million view,

00:44:22.950 --> 00:44:25.365
a million subscribers around that time.

