So that was like the
course of a year, man.

00:44:43.300 --> 00:44:44.380
How's that possible?

00:44:44.380 --> 00:44:46.780
No, it was two years.

00:44:46.780 --> 00:44:48.950
So for those two years, still that's the-

00:44:48.950 --> 00:44:51.530
January, 2014, we had a million subs.

00:44:51.530 --> 00:44:52.970
January 20...

00:44:52.970 --> 00:44:57.970
Yeah, January of 2016 is when
we had 10 million subscribers.

00:44:58.330 --> 00:45:01.108
So yeah, that's when it
really started to pick up.

00:45:01.108 --> 00:45:03.440
I mean, I remember the
thing that I was thinking

00:45:03.440 --> 00:45:08.440
at this time is that I had always seen GMM

00:45:09.150 --> 00:45:11.840
as what I called the side project, right?

00:45:11.840 --> 00:45:14.400
I mean, that's why we put
it on the second channel.

00:45:14.400 --> 00:45:15.233
Yeah.

00:45:15.233 --> 00:45:17.190
To this time, we're still doing like,

00:45:17.190 --> 00:45:19.630
sketches, music videos,
and that kind of thing.

00:45:19.630 --> 00:45:20.900
But...

00:45:20.900 --> 00:45:24.290
This was the year that,

00:45:24.290 --> 00:45:26.899
that two year period, 2014 to 2015,

00:45:26.899 --> 00:45:31.899
it was where GMM surpassed in
anything that we were doing

00:45:33.738 --> 00:45:35.090
on the Rhett and Link channel,

00:45:35.090 --> 00:45:37.180
on the main channel in
terms of just the level

00:45:37.180 --> 00:45:38.340
of engagement and the number,

00:45:38.340 --> 00:45:39.850
at least the number of subscribers,

00:45:39.850 --> 00:45:42.360
and just a fan base that
was building around it.

00:45:42.360 --> 00:45:43.193
Yeah.

00:45:43.193 --> 00:45:44.940
And I think both of us were thinking like,

00:45:44.940 --> 00:45:47.669
oh man, this is becoming our thing.

00:45:47.669 --> 00:45:49.920
This is not a side project.

00:45:49.920 --> 00:45:51.680
Yeah, so a lot more focus,

00:45:51.680 --> 00:45:52.860
so much so that we were like,

00:45:52.860 --> 00:45:55.610
let's make a Hawkman
trailer for a Hawkman movie

00:45:55.610 --> 00:45:58.670
that doesn't exist in hopes that like,

00:45:58.670 --> 00:45:59.820
people will care about that.

00:45:59.820 --> 00:46:00.980
They didn't really.
They did not.

00:46:00.980 --> 00:46:04.181
Episode 82, "Will it Taco?"

00:46:04.181 --> 00:46:08.290
Episode 88, sensory deprivation tank.

00:46:08.290 --> 00:46:11.760
So it's like we, we had just
hatched the will it series,

00:46:11.760 --> 00:46:14.803
and the sensory deprivation tank was,

00:46:15.720 --> 00:46:17.440
so okay, we're gonna go out into the world

00:46:17.440 --> 00:46:18.273
and do some stuff.

00:46:18.273 --> 00:46:19.490
We didn't do it that often,

00:46:19.490 --> 00:46:20.920
but it was a really good episode.

00:46:20.920 --> 00:46:22.993
Well, before moving past "Will it Taco?"

00:46:22.993 --> 00:46:24.883
It's got 20 million views now.

00:46:26.009 --> 00:46:28.130
Was this the...

00:46:28.130 --> 00:46:31.970
Up until this point I
don't know if we had done,

00:46:31.970 --> 00:46:34.940
like the next time we did
will it after this was when,

00:46:34.940 --> 00:46:38.143
because up to this point, we
didn't see things as series.

00:46:39.100 --> 00:46:39.933
Yeah.
Right?

00:46:39.933 --> 00:46:41.310
I don't see any evidence.

00:46:41.310 --> 00:46:42.730
It was always like, kind of,

00:46:42.730 --> 00:46:44.410
okay, maybe this is a slight twist

00:46:44.410 --> 00:46:46.303
on something that we did,
or we're playing a game,

00:46:46.303 --> 00:46:51.303
but we didn't have a title
that just changed out one word.

00:46:52.470 --> 00:46:53.630
Like, "Will it Taco?"

00:46:53.630 --> 00:46:55.490
Oh, now let's do, "Will
it Burrito?" or whatever.

00:46:55.490 --> 00:46:57.750
And so that was Cinco de Mayo.

00:46:57.750 --> 00:47:00.260
In July, we did "Will
it Ice Cream Sandwich?"

00:47:00.260 --> 00:47:03.740
Which was in the next season six.

00:47:03.740 --> 00:47:08.380
Okay, so it took us a full
season to come back to...

00:47:08.380 --> 00:47:09.600
That's interesting.

00:47:09.600 --> 00:47:10.763
Again, we weren't seeing, like-

00:47:10.763 --> 00:47:12.670
It took us two months, yeah.

00:47:12.670 --> 00:47:13.570
But we weren't...

00:47:13.570 --> 00:47:16.780
And we're just way
different these days where

00:47:18.743 --> 00:47:22.100
we're constantly trying
to come up with an idea

00:47:22.100 --> 00:47:24.240
that then can be a series,

00:47:24.240 --> 00:47:27.300
because we just found that
that's what people like.

00:47:27.300 --> 00:47:28.375
I mean, obviously there's

00:47:28.375 --> 00:47:31.350
production considerations for that.

00:47:31.350 --> 00:47:32.390
You get something that works,

00:47:32.390 --> 00:47:34.410
you want to do it again
because the team knows

00:47:34.410 --> 00:47:35.780
how to produce that,

00:47:35.780 --> 00:47:38.140
but also it develops a life of it's own,

00:47:38.140 --> 00:47:40.880
like the international dart
game has, at this point,

00:47:40.880 --> 00:47:42.850
which I'm sure you'll talk about
the first time we did that,

00:47:42.850 --> 00:47:43.683
eventually.

00:47:43.683 --> 00:47:47.390
But we weren't thinking
about the show in that way,

00:47:47.390 --> 00:47:48.260
at this time.

00:47:48.260 --> 00:47:49.204
Yeah, at the end,

00:47:49.204 --> 00:47:50.700
over the course of season five,

00:47:50.700 --> 00:47:51.533
the other thing we did

00:47:51.533 --> 00:47:55.450
was wheel of mythicality animations,

00:47:55.450 --> 00:47:57.023
we started releasing those.

00:47:58.040 --> 00:48:01.194
And then season six, July of 2014,

00:48:01.194 --> 00:48:04.660
that's when we got our
new intro with the column

00:48:04.660 --> 00:48:05.910
where it starts at night, and like,

00:48:05.910 --> 00:48:07.661
it's going up the column.

00:48:07.661 --> 00:48:10.950
We still had some more
animations coming out.

00:48:10.950 --> 00:48:14.093
Episode nine of season
six, that's when we did the

00:48:14.093 --> 00:48:15.902
vacay gone cray-cay.

00:48:15.902 --> 00:48:17.600
Cray-cay.
Cray-cay.

00:48:17.600 --> 00:48:18.797
Cray-cray,

00:48:18.797 --> 00:48:23.310
where we would re-enact stories

00:48:23.310 --> 00:48:25.290
of people's vacations gone wrong,

00:48:25.290 --> 00:48:28.090
which was sponsored by the
same people that sponsored

00:48:29.356 --> 00:48:32.390
"I'm on Vacation," the music video.

00:48:32.390 --> 00:48:33.860
Post someone at a hotel?

00:48:33.860 --> 00:48:34.730
Choice hotels?

00:48:34.730 --> 00:48:35.563
Yeah.
But yeah,

00:48:35.563 --> 00:48:37.632
in that episode nine,

00:48:37.632 --> 00:48:39.270
it was also on a Thursday,

00:48:39.270 --> 00:48:41.100
that's when we would also do mail.

00:48:41.100 --> 00:48:43.977
So we started having variety episodes

00:48:43.977 --> 00:48:47.330
where we would do a little something,

00:48:47.330 --> 00:48:50.720
usually a prompt from a fan,

00:48:50.720 --> 00:48:55.170
and then we would go into the
Vacay Gone Cray-Cray segment,

00:48:55.170 --> 00:48:58.443
because we wanted to be
able to sell to a sponsor

00:48:58.443 --> 00:49:00.526
a segment within an episode,

00:49:00.526 --> 00:49:03.330
but then do other things that we could use

00:49:03.330 --> 00:49:06.400
to market the episode
with title and thumbnail,

00:49:06.400 --> 00:49:08.797
and we would add mail to it.

00:49:08.797 --> 00:49:11.560
And then, so Jen would bring out the mail,

00:49:11.560 --> 00:49:14.680
but she wasn't on camera, and
it was in the main episode.

00:49:14.680 --> 00:49:15.540
She wasn't on camera?

00:49:15.540 --> 00:49:17.057
She wasn't on camera.

00:49:17.057 --> 00:49:19.300
And we did sing the song.

00:49:19.300 --> 00:49:21.390
Yeah, Thursday means mail.

00:49:21.390 --> 00:49:23.520
And you're talking season six?

00:49:23.520 --> 00:49:24.690
Yeah.

00:49:24.690 --> 00:49:25.523
Episode nine?

00:49:25.523 --> 00:49:26.500
Episode nine.

00:49:26.500 --> 00:49:27.700
Episode 17-

00:49:27.700 --> 00:49:30.637
Okay, because we still called that,

00:49:30.637 --> 00:49:32.530
"Outrageous Camping Gear You Must Own."

00:49:32.530 --> 00:49:35.420
And yeah, because the first
thing we talked about was-

00:49:35.420 --> 00:49:38.400
Which got 5.6 million views.
Outrageous camping gear.

00:49:38.400 --> 00:49:40.630
Again, the lists were working for us.

00:49:40.630 --> 00:49:42.715
No one was gonna click
on watch us re-enact

00:49:42.715 --> 00:49:44.442
somebodies bad vacation,

00:49:44.442 --> 00:49:48.250
but once we got the click
with the crazy looking tents.

00:49:48.250 --> 00:49:50.450
So we were figuring out those things.

00:49:50.450 --> 00:49:54.130
It's like, if we can do a
variety episode every week,

00:49:54.130 --> 00:49:55.130
we can learn more,

00:49:55.130 --> 00:49:56.700
we can do more creative things,

00:49:56.700 --> 00:49:59.470
and we can connect with
the mythical beasts

00:49:59.470 --> 00:50:01.150
by reading their mail.

00:50:01.150 --> 00:50:06.150
Episodes 17 is when we
went to the YouTube space,

00:50:06.460 --> 00:50:08.720
and we had Daniel Radcliffe on the show.

00:50:08.720 --> 00:50:09.553
Up until this point,

00:50:09.553 --> 00:50:11.540
we really hadn't had guests on the show.

00:50:11.540 --> 00:50:16.300
We had had guests appear
on "The Mythical Show,"

00:50:16.300 --> 00:50:18.960
but then we didn't add any
guests when we went back

00:50:18.960 --> 00:50:20.285
to "Good Mythical Morning,"

00:50:20.285 --> 00:50:22.470
but we couldn't turn
down Daniel Radcliffe,

00:50:22.470 --> 00:50:24.480
and I just remember being
so freaking nervous.

00:50:24.480 --> 00:50:25.490
Like, I still can't.

00:50:25.490 --> 00:50:27.010
I wouldn't watch that episode back.

00:50:27.010 --> 00:50:28.550
Well, it's not only that,

00:50:28.550 --> 00:50:30.950
we wanted it to,

00:50:30.950 --> 00:50:34.320
first of all, we had this hang up,

00:50:34.320 --> 00:50:38.335
and we still do have it
where we were like, okay,

00:50:38.335 --> 00:50:42.990
when a celebrity comes
to the YouTube space,

00:50:42.990 --> 00:50:44.730
and other YouTubers go to it,

00:50:44.730 --> 00:50:46.160
it's almost like a press junket,

00:50:46.160 --> 00:50:47.731
and they're just do making videos.

00:50:47.731 --> 00:50:50.240
For us, it felt a little cheap, right?

00:50:50.240 --> 00:50:52.360
Because we were like,
"Man, we want our show

00:50:52.360 --> 00:50:55.080
to feel like a place that
celebrities want to come

00:50:55.080 --> 00:50:56.110
and actually be on,

00:50:56.110 --> 00:50:57.500
because that's what a legitimate show is."

00:50:57.500 --> 00:50:59.970
Jimmy Fallon doesn't go and go somewhere,

00:50:59.970 --> 00:51:00.803
you come to his show.

00:51:00.803 --> 00:51:01.770
That had never happened,

00:51:01.770 --> 00:51:03.910
but we said that's how we
would want it to happen.

00:51:03.910 --> 00:51:08.910
But the compromise was, we're
going to print out our set.

00:51:09.900 --> 00:51:11.890
No, Paisley actually built it.

00:51:11.890 --> 00:51:13.280
He built it like.

00:51:13.280 --> 00:51:14.420
Oh, yeah.
Paper mache,

00:51:14.420 --> 00:51:15.760
it was like-
Yes.

00:51:15.760 --> 00:51:17.410
Paper mosaic.
Yes.

00:51:17.410 --> 00:51:20.420
It was really amazing what he did,

00:51:20.420 --> 00:51:22.360
and I don't even think
it came across on camera,

00:51:22.360 --> 00:51:24.670
but your eyes forget that
we're not in front of our

00:51:24.670 --> 00:51:25.503
own set.
Yeah,

00:51:25.503 --> 00:51:27.280
so we did basically a portable set,

00:51:27.280 --> 00:51:28.240
which was a whole lot of work.

00:51:28.240 --> 00:51:31.770
Later when we had to do the
same thing another time,

00:51:31.770 --> 00:51:32.920
we printed it out.

00:51:32.920 --> 00:51:35.380
But yeah, I forgot the
first one was a literal.

00:51:35.380 --> 00:51:36.850
He unrolled the thing.

00:51:36.850 --> 00:51:37.683
It was crazy.
It unrolled.

00:51:37.683 --> 00:51:39.110
Yeah, it's crazy.

00:51:39.110 --> 00:51:40.520
And then we had to sit around for hours

00:51:40.520 --> 00:51:42.660
for Daniel Radcliffe to show up.

00:51:42.660 --> 00:51:43.820
And he was a joy.

00:51:43.820 --> 00:51:45.130
He was a joy.
He was a joy.

00:51:45.130 --> 00:51:46.893
Episode 56.

00:51:46.893 --> 00:51:49.280
That was the Carolina Reaper.

00:51:49.280 --> 00:51:52.510
That's still the thing that
is more often than anything

00:51:52.510 --> 00:51:55.410
the thing that people
talk about if they see us

00:51:55.410 --> 00:51:56.400
out on the street.

00:51:56.400 --> 00:51:59.450
Episode 110 was our first weirdest E-bay,

00:51:59.450 --> 00:52:00.660
where Stevie was-
Oh, really?

00:52:00.660 --> 00:52:01.493
The host.

00:52:01.493 --> 00:52:02.810
Well, okay, so Stevie,

00:52:02.810 --> 00:52:03.840
yeah.
Wrapping up

00:52:03.840 --> 00:52:05.080
2014.
At what point

00:52:05.080 --> 00:52:08.990
did Stevie start becoming
the voice of the goddess

00:52:08.990 --> 00:52:10.143
off camera?

00:52:11.084 --> 00:52:12.949
I don't know.

00:52:12.949 --> 00:52:17.190
'Cause I know that
season four, episode 64,

00:52:17.190 --> 00:52:19.303
we did the movie setting game,

00:52:20.520 --> 00:52:22.567
which was the first time that we had...

00:52:22.567 --> 00:52:25.580
We're like, let's put
a title screen on this.

00:52:25.580 --> 00:52:27.150
We still didn't say, "It's time for,"

00:52:27.150 --> 00:52:29.020
but we called it something impromptu,

00:52:29.020 --> 00:52:30.670
and like Jason made a title screen.

00:52:30.670 --> 00:52:35.096
Jason was the off-screen
voice for those games,

00:52:35.096 --> 00:52:37.210
so I don't know exactly
when that switched,

00:52:37.210 --> 00:52:39.840
but by this point, Stevie was not only,

00:52:39.840 --> 00:52:42.950
she did that on camera what
was doing stuff off camera,

00:52:42.950 --> 00:52:44.960
I'm sure, by that point.

00:52:44.960 --> 00:52:47.400
So then let's go to season seven.

00:52:47.400 --> 00:52:48.233
All right.

00:52:48.233 --> 00:52:53.233
January 2015, we had a
new wheel with 24 spaces.

00:52:53.354 --> 00:52:55.740
That was a big moment.
Yeah.

00:52:55.740 --> 00:52:59.047
We would have variety episodes that were,

00:52:59.047 --> 00:53:01.109
they were so question-based,

00:53:01.109 --> 00:53:04.670
so I remember that we would take questions

00:53:04.670 --> 00:53:07.290
from mythical beast
and we would use those,

00:53:07.290 --> 00:53:10.983
the writers would then
pitch us comedy bits to do.

00:53:10.983 --> 00:53:15.782
Like someone gave feedback on how I was,

00:53:15.782 --> 00:53:19.450
like, we took a comment about
how I made Eddie eat something

00:53:19.450 --> 00:53:20.360
that he didn't want to eat,

00:53:20.360 --> 00:53:22.430
and I was kind of being a jerk to him.

00:53:22.430 --> 00:53:24.376
And so they were like, you were like,

00:53:24.376 --> 00:53:25.457
yeah, it actually happens a lot,

00:53:25.457 --> 00:53:28.870
and we cut to a sketch
of hidden camera footage

00:53:28.870 --> 00:53:31.508
of me being a tyrant around the studio.

00:53:31.508 --> 00:53:34.040
So we were still trying to
all different types of things

00:53:34.040 --> 00:53:35.605
in like these many variety

00:53:35.605 --> 00:53:36.670
episodes.
It got 5 million views,

00:53:36.670 --> 00:53:38.679
or it does at this point.

00:53:38.679 --> 00:53:40.916
'Cause we called it "Link Is A Tyrant."

00:53:40.916 --> 00:53:43.377
We also started "Song Biscuits."

00:53:44.380 --> 00:53:45.543
So this was a new thing.

00:53:45.543 --> 00:53:46.376
It was like, all right,

00:53:46.376 --> 00:53:47.580
not just doing an "Ear Biscuit,"

00:53:47.580 --> 00:53:49.150
and having them come on the show.

00:53:49.150 --> 00:53:50.810
But that was a weekend series.

00:53:50.810 --> 00:53:52.590
Yeah, but we got...

00:53:52.590 --> 00:53:53.820
I mean, that was ambitious.

00:53:53.820 --> 00:53:54.837
That was kind of a,

00:53:54.837 --> 00:53:56.250
"Hey, you're gonna come on a podcast,

00:53:56.250 --> 00:53:59.240
and then you're gonna
write a song with us."

00:53:59.240 --> 00:54:00.910
I wouldn't have said yes to that.

00:54:00.910 --> 00:54:02.510
We made it easy for people, man.

00:54:02.510 --> 00:54:04.342
They didn't have to do much.
Yeah, but,

00:54:04.342 --> 00:54:06.970
I was like, man, that was
asking a lot of people.

00:54:06.970 --> 00:54:08.010
But, okay.

00:54:08.010 --> 00:54:09.720
Yeah, and like you said before that,

00:54:09.720 --> 00:54:12.640
there was the wheel of
mythicality animations again.

00:54:12.640 --> 00:54:16.180
So, I'm thinking about
where this decision leads.

00:54:16.180 --> 00:54:17.840
That's one of the
fascinating things for me

00:54:17.840 --> 00:54:19.499
is that we make a decision

00:54:19.499 --> 00:54:21.650
for whatever reason we
were making it at the time,

00:54:21.650 --> 00:54:25.260
and then just making the decision

00:54:25.260 --> 00:54:26.460
then leads to something else.

00:54:26.460 --> 00:54:28.730
So I would say that decisions like this

00:54:28.730 --> 00:54:31.470
to do song biscuits on the weekend...

00:54:32.540 --> 00:54:35.750
Okay, maybe what we
were thinking, I dunno,

00:54:35.750 --> 00:54:38.150
one of the things we
were thinking was man,

00:54:38.150 --> 00:54:40.070
like we've gotten to this point

00:54:40.070 --> 00:54:41.020
where we're putting so much time

00:54:41.020 --> 00:54:42.580
into "Good Mythical Morning."

00:54:42.580 --> 00:54:45.730
It doesn't really justify
itself to put all this time

00:54:45.730 --> 00:54:48.540
into a music video on our main channel,

00:54:48.540 --> 00:54:50.169
unless it's sponsored.

00:54:50.169 --> 00:54:53.860
And even then sometimes it
would be weeks or months of work

00:54:53.860 --> 00:54:55.350
for one piece of content, right?

00:54:55.350 --> 00:54:58.150
Whereas we can do as well with GMM.

00:54:58.150 --> 00:54:59.070
So we were like, okay,

00:54:59.070 --> 00:55:01.020
well we're still really
good at writing songs.

00:55:01.020 --> 00:55:02.647
Let's make it something
that's more interactive,

00:55:02.647 --> 00:55:06.460
and quicker, and that's what
led to doing Song Biscuits,

00:55:06.460 --> 00:55:08.070
and hey, why didn't we put that

00:55:08.070 --> 00:55:09.970
on the Rhett and Link channel?

00:55:09.970 --> 00:55:12.455
Well, again, at this point in season seven

00:55:12.455 --> 00:55:16.300
there's all this traction
on "Good Mythical Morning,"

00:55:16.300 --> 00:55:19.070
so it's like, this is the place
that people's eyeballs are,

00:55:19.070 --> 00:55:20.770
so let's put it on the weekend,

00:55:20.770 --> 00:55:22.858
on the GMM channel.

00:55:22.858 --> 00:55:27.858
That decision led to things
like mythical kitchen, right?

00:55:29.690 --> 00:55:31.490
Because mythical kitchen,

00:55:31.490 --> 00:55:34.788
before it was mythical
kitchen, it was a weekend show,

